WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.060
As action flicks and superhero blockbusters
continue to dominate the box office, we're

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:09.130
finally getting the strong female leads we've
been lacking for decades in both film and

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:10.130
TV.

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:13.310
The physical demands of these roles are no
joke, but these actresses were more than up

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:14.390
for the challenge.

00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:18.080
Let's take a look at some of the amazing women
who put in maximum effort in order to kick

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:19.869
ass onscreen.

00:00:19.869 --> 00:00:21.100
Alison Brie

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:25.810
Until recently, Alison Brie was best known
for playing a long-suffering wife on Mad Men

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:29.150
— a role that required serious acting skills,
but no stunt work.

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:33.370
So when she landed a starring role on Netflix's
original series GLOW, she had to train like

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:35.670
a madwoman to get in literal fighting shape.

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:39.899
Sometimes, that meant intense workouts where
she hurled weighted objects onto the gym floor;

00:00:39.899 --> 00:00:44.840
other times, it meant carrying her 220-pound
trainer, Jason Walsh, around the room on her

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:45.840
back.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:48.670
Walsh said his goal for the training regimen
was to turn Brie into someone who could both

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:50.210
dish out and take a hit.

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:51.719
He told Business Insider,

00:00:51.719 --> 00:00:53.129
"Alison did all her stunts.

00:00:53.129 --> 00:00:57.390
I'll tell you right now, I've worked with
a lot of people and she's a little bad a--."

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.050
Alicia Vikander

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:03.890
Prior to her preparation for the role of adventure
junkie Lara Croft in the Tomb Raider reboot,

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:06.280
Alicia Vikander told The Graham Norton Show,

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:09.159
"I had never lifted a thing with my arms."

00:01:09.159 --> 00:01:13.430
Not wanting to disappoint fans, Vikander hit
the gym harder than ever for four months.

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:17.390
The Oscar-winner ended up adding 10 to 12
pounds of muscle, but this new and improved

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:18.640
physique would be short-lived.

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:22.100
"It takes three weeks for you to lose it all.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:24.570
That is the sad bit."

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:26.600
Lupita Nyong'o

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:30.159
Someone forgot to tell Lupita Nyong'O you're
not supposed to enjoy bootcamp.

00:01:30.159 --> 00:01:34.141
She took part in a six-week session along
with her Black Panther co-stars — sometimes

00:01:34.141 --> 00:01:39.020
working out as early as 3 a.m., for as long
as four hours — and called the intense experience

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:40.020
"fun."

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:43.210
Nyong'O told Collider she enjoyed challenging
her body, saying,

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:45.520
"I get to jump higher than I thought I could
jump.

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:49.320
[...] I get to roll backwards, which I thought
I would never do after the age of 8?

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:50.320
So it's been fun."

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:54.810
Nyong'O was already a workout enthusiast,
but the exercising and dieting for Black Panther

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:57.009
took her fitness to a whole other level.

00:01:57.009 --> 00:01:58.200
She told The Hollywood Reporter,

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:02.590
"I remember coming home for Christmas and
I couldn't fit into my clothes."

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:04.109
Margot Robbie

00:02:04.109 --> 00:02:08.899
Director Craig Gillespie pulled off skating
scenes in I, Tonya using both CGI and stunt

00:02:08.899 --> 00:02:12.540
doubles, but not all of Margot Robbie's scenes
involved Hollywood magic.

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:16.210
She trained on the ice three times a week
for three months and learned five routines

00:02:16.210 --> 00:02:17.210
in all.

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:19.000
Robbie told Wonderland of her intense training,

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:22.790
"My alarm would go off at 5:30 a.m. and I'd
want to cry.

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:25.430
Sometimes after sessions I'd get back into
the car and weep."

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:29.150
Those tears of frustration eventually turned
into tears of joy.

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:33.409
Robbie's performance as the disgraced skater
earned her an Oscar nomination.

00:02:33.409 --> 00:02:35.069
Emma Stone

00:02:35.069 --> 00:02:38.770
Trainer Jason Walsh has an Instagram photo
of a feeble Emma Stone with a caption that

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:40.730
reads "Deadlift PR day.

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:44.560
Change takes breaking comfort" and states
that Stone was prepping for her role in Battle

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:45.560
of the Sexes.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:46.860
He told W Magazine,

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:50.980
"When she trained for La La Land, we worked
out three to four days a week.

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:55.069
With Battle of the Sexes we did five days
a week and sometimes two times a day."

00:02:55.069 --> 00:02:59.060
Stone trained for three months and put on
15 pounds of muscle for the role.

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:01.080
She seemed giddy with the results, telling
CNN:

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:05.150
"It was the first time I'd ever felt like,
'Oh my god, I can lift a lot of weight.'

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:07.000
[…] You feel like the Hulk, a little bit."

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:11.670
"It was the first time I focused so, so much
on the physicality of someone, because playing

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:16.540
an athlete… that is the way she was able
to make change in the world."

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:18.080
Rooney Mara

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:21.940
It wasn't enough for Rooney Mara to get multiple
piercings for her role in The Girl with the

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:23.180
Dragon Tattoo.

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:27.489
She was determined to go all in, which, for
her, meant training in a wide variety of fields.

00:03:27.489 --> 00:03:28.569
She told MTV,

00:03:28.569 --> 00:03:30.010
"I feel like I went to school.

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:35.269
I had motorcycle class from 9 to 11, and then
I went to dialect class, and then I had skateboarding,

00:03:35.269 --> 00:03:38.180
and then I had computer training, and then
I had kickboxing."

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:40.450
She told the Hollywood Reporter the skateboarding
was…

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:43.209
"...to sort of try and change the way that
I walk and stand."

00:03:43.209 --> 00:03:46.970
The kickboxing was meant to help her feel
confident taking her clothes off on screen.

00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:47.970
She told Parade,

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:51.970
"The character is incredibly comfortable in
her sexuality, and I had to go in making the

00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:53.650
film feeling the same way."

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:55.300
Thanks for watching!

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:57.939
